WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.246
"We must rest," Long John said, collapsing on the ground when we finally got to the top of the plateau.

2
00:00:08.247 --> 00:00:13.875
The land descended toward the west, and we all sat and admired the view around us.

3
00:00:13.876 --> 00:00:20.385
Not a sail was upon the sea, and the vastness of the view increased our sense of solitude.

4
00:00:20.386 --> 00:00:27.542
The only sound was the distant surf from Cape of the Woods and the nearby chirp of insects.

5
00:00:27.543 --> 00:00:33.620
"Nothing stops the sea," Dick said. "It makes me feel very alone."

6
00:00:33.621 --> 00:00:36.050
Long John took bearings with his compass.

7
00:00:36.051 --> 00:00:42.076
"There are three ‘tall trees’ in a direct line from Skeleton Island.

8
00:00:42.077 --> 00:00:46.344
‘Spyglass shoulder’ means that lower point there.

9
00:00:46.345 --> 00:00:49.608
It’s simple to find the treasure now."

10
00:00:49.609 --> 00:00:56.879
"I don’t feel so good," Morgan growled. "Thinking of Flint has upset me."

11
00:00:56.880 --> 00:01:02.240
"Just be thankful he’s dead," said Long John in a low voice.

12
00:01:02.241 --> 00:01:09.555
"He was an ugly devil," another pirate whispered with a shudder, "and his face was blue!"

13
00:01:09.556 --> 00:01:13.878
"The rum did that," George Merry whispered back.

14
00:01:13.879 --> 00:01:20.390
All of a sudden, a thin, high, trembling voice struck up a well-known tune:

15
00:01:20.391 --> 00:01:29.067
"Fifteen men on a dead man’s chest— Yo-ho-ho, and a bottle of rum!"

16
00:01:29.068 --> 00:01:32.289
The song stopped as suddenly as it began.

17
00:01:32.290 --> 00:01:36.586
Instantly, the color drained from every pirate’s face.

18
00:01:36.587 --> 00:01:42.758
Two leaped to their feet, and the man with the bandaged head grabbed at the pirate next to him in fear.

19
00:01:42.759 --> 00:01:47.809
Tom Morgan crawled on the ground, trying to find a place to hide.

20
00:01:47.810 --> 00:01:53.368
"It’s Flint!" George Merry cried. "His ghost walks!"

21
00:01:53.369 --> 00:02:00.987
"Come now, this won’t do," croaked Long John, struggling to get the words out with ashen lips.

22
00:02:00.988 --> 00:02:12.025
"I don’t recognize the voice, but someone’s trying to scare us—someone who’s flesh and blood."

23
00:02:12.026 --> 00:02:17.634
Long John’s courage came back as he spoke, and the others nodded, less fearful now.

24
00:02:17.635 --> 00:02:26.799
But then the same voice broke out again—not in song, but in a faint call that echoed among the cliffs of Spyglass Hill.

25
00:02:26.800 --> 00:02:34.204
"Darby McGraw, Darby McGraw!" it wailed again and again.

26
00:02:34.205 --> 00:02:41.903
Then, rising a little higher, it said, "Fetch the rum, Darby!"

27
00:02:41.904 --> 00:02:45.787
The pirates remained rooted to the ground, their eyes bulging.

28
00:02:45.788 --> 00:02:50.499
Long after the voice had died away, they stared in silence.

29
00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:55.741
"That does it!" one gasped. "Let’s get out of here."

30
00:02:55.742 --> 00:02:59.169
"Those were his last words," Tom Morgan moaned.

31
00:02:59.170 --> 00:03:05.043
"Flint died asking for more rum. Nobody but us knows that!"

32
00:03:05.044 --> 00:03:11.104
Dick took his Bible out and knelt. "Our Father," he started to pray.

33
00:03:11.105 --> 00:03:15.244
Long John was shivering, but he wasn’t about to surrender.

34
00:03:15.245 --> 00:03:23.185
"Flint never scared me in his life, and by thunder, he doesn’t scare me now that he’s dead.

35
00:03:23.186 --> 00:03:31.575
There’s seven hundred thousand dollars worth of gold not a quarter of a mile from here.

36
00:03:31.576 --> 00:03:34.609
Who’s going to turn his back on that?

37
00:03:34.610 --> 00:03:42.599
Flint was a drunken, old seaman with a blue face—and he’s dead!"

38
00:03:42.600 --> 00:03:50.114
"Stop talking like that, Long John!" George Merry hissed. "Don’t insult a ghost." They

39
00:03:50.115 --> 00:03:54.409
huddled around Long John, as if his courage could protect them. "Ghost?

40
00:03:54.410 --> 00:04:09.284
Well, maybe," answered Long John. "But I heard an echo too. No ghost has a shadow. So what’s he doing with an echo?" I

41
00:04:09.285 --> 00:04:15.362
thought it was a weak argument, but one can never tell what superstitious people will believe. However,

42
00:04:15.363 --> 00:04:20.244
George Merry was greatly relieved. "You’re right, Long John! Come

43
00:04:20.245 --> 00:04:26.775
to think, it was like Flint’s voice, but not as clear. It was like—" "By

44
00:04:26.776 --> 00:04:32.330
thunder—Ben Gunn!" roared Long John. "Aye,"

45
00:04:32.331 --> 00:04:38.465
shouted Tom Morgan. "It was Ben Gunn!" "What?"

46
00:04:38.466 --> 00:04:44.324
said Dick. "Ben Gunn’s not here any more than Flint is." "Ah,

47
00:04:44.325 --> 00:04:49.208
Dick, who’s to say he’s not?" George Merry cried. "He

48
00:04:49.209 --> 00:04:54.797
was left here, but he still might be alive after all this time." "That’s

49
00:04:54.798 --> 00:04:58.438
right!" agreed the man with the head wound. Their

50
00:04:58.439 --> 00:05:03.851
spirits soared, and the pirates grabbed their tools and started off again. George

51
00:05:03.852 --> 00:05:08.107
Merry led with the compass to keep them on the right course. But

52
00:05:08.108 --> 00:05:14.200
Dick, who was very scared and feeling more ill from his malaria, still held his Bible. "You

53
00:05:14.201 --> 00:05:21.874
spoiled your Bible. It can’t protect you now," said Long John with a sly grin. All

54
00:05:21.875 --> 00:05:27.208
of us started walking downhill through the pines, great and small. "Two

55
00:05:27.209 --> 00:05:33.155
of these tall trees are wrong by the compass bearings," Long John said. "But

56
00:05:33.156 --> 00:05:39.190
that third tree is tall enough, almost two hundred feet. It

57
00:05:39.191 --> 00:05:44.252
must have been a landmark for sailors out at sea." The

58
00:05:44.253 --> 00:05:48.171
thought of the treasure erased their fear and they started to run. A

59
00:05:48.172 --> 00:05:53.103
whole lifetime of riches and pleasure lay waiting for them. Long

60
00:05:53.104 --> 00:06:02.607
John hobbled on his crutch. His nostrils quivered, and he cursed like a madman as he pulled my leash. "Come on, boy!" "He’s

61
00:06:02.608 --> 00:06:05.433
not even pretending," I said to myself. "He’ll

62
00:06:05.434 --> 00:06:11.997
seize the treasure, find the Hispaniola , cut every honest throat, and sail away."

63
00:06:11.998 --> 00:06:17.255
I was too haunted by the human tragedy that had happened here to keep up with the pirates.

64
00:06:17.256 --> 00:06:21.848
"How this peaceful place must have echoed with screams!" I thought.

65
00:06:21.849 --> 00:06:26.284
Long John jerked the rope again and gave me another murderous look.

66
00:06:26.285 --> 00:06:30.859
Dick dropped farther behind as his fever got worse.

67
00:06:30.860 --> 00:06:33.810
We were now at the edge of the woods.

68
00:06:33.811 --> 00:06:38.180
"Hurry, mates! Run!" George Merry shouted up ahead.

69
00:06:38.181 --> 00:06:44.306
And suddenly, not ten yards further, the men stopped and a low cry arose.

70
00:06:44.307 --> 00:06:49.216
Long John doubled his pace, pounding through the dirt with his crutch until finally

71
00:06:49.217 --> 00:06:55.048
he and I came to a dead halt as we joined the others before a huge hole.

72
00:06:55.049 --> 00:07:01.079
"It’s old," I thought. "The sides have fallen in, and grass is growing on the bottom."

73
00:07:01.080 --> 00:07:05.501
Then I saw a broken pick and the boards of several packing cases.

74
00:07:05.502 --> 00:07:10.190
One board was branded "Walrus"—the name of Flint’s ship.

75
00:07:10.191 --> 00:07:19.378
George Merry choked. "Someone beat us to it. The treasure’s gone!"

